# An xor of thread index fields reads as one variable, the xor of its
# runs of thread bits; added to the shared base it is the address
# (micro/xor_swizzle.ptx, whose stored offsets an RTX 4090 reads back as
# its header gives). One side of micro_xor_overlap's xor is a sum whose
# fields share a bit, which is no xor of them, and stays unknown.
RUN: %ptxroof analyze %fixtures/micro/xor_swizzle.ptx | FileCheck "%s"
CHECK: kernel micro_xor_swizzle
CHECK: <block 0>  st.shared.u32  shared store 4 B  warp: 4 wavefronts (ideal 1)   [(16 * (⌊%tid.x/8⌋ mod 4) ⊕ 16 * (%tid.x mod 128)) + buf + 64]
CHECK: kernel micro_xor_overlap
CHECK: <block 0>  st.shared.u32  shared store 4 B                                 unknown: depends on special register %tid.x, behind `xor.b32`
